+/// The Adaptive stock band in tool radii (plus [`OPEN_SLACK`]): the
+/// tool centre reaches a full radius past the stock, the air entry disc
+/// clear of it (issue #1950).
+pub const ADAPTIVE_BAND_PER_R: f64 = 2.0;
+
+/// The stock band of `open_sides` for a tool of radius `r`: the
+/// Adaptive one (`adaptive`), else the open band every strategy had.
+pub fn stock_band(r: f64, adaptive: bool) -> f64 {
+    if adaptive { ADAPTIVE_BAND_PER_R * r + OPEN_SLACK } else { r - OPEN_SLACK }
+}

From 746eabff3ba99b01c08747a007fa10901409b124 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:58:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] feat(app): whole-model Adaptive 3D Pocket plans its
 stock ring from the air

The Adaptive plain ladder of a whole-model 3D Pocket now reaches
stock_band(r, true) past the stock and calls pocket3d_open_prev with
the stock outline. Shell, rest and Multi-Axis Rough keep the old band.
Pinned by a_clamp_in_the_air_band_blocks_the_post: steel in the air
band is struck and the post gate names it.

Refs #1950

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
